1
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:05,740
Let's pretend yesterday

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,830
never happened.

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:07,910
Okay!

4
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:09,290
Huh?

5
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:16,379
Let's just pretend it never happened.

6
00:00:16,379 --> 00:00:18,380
What do you mean by that?

7
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,220
Okay, got it.

8
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:34,900
Sigh.

9
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:42,610
Jae-on.

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,620
Let's call it a day.

11
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:46,950
Uh...

12
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:50,790
Shouldn't we talk to Director Jung?

13
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:53,670
Uh, he seemed busy.
He said we can leave.

14
00:00:58,290 --> 00:00:59,050
Sorry.

15
00:00:59,050 --> 00:00:59,800
No problem.

16
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:05,390
There's a leak on the unit above yours.

17
00:01:05,390 --> 00:01:07,390
Your unit's completely flooded.

18
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:08,300
I couldn't reach you,

19
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,640
so I moved all your stuff out.

20
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,140
Until it dries, you have to
sleep somewhere else tonight.

21
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,850
Wait, how am I supposed to
find a place this late...

22
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:16,150
Here.

23
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,570
Can I sleep here?

24
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:22,940
Of course, you can.

25
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:26,240
Our great actor Kang
needs his beauty sleep!

26
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,910
Make yourself at home.

27
00:01:28,539 --> 00:01:29,500
It's all yours.

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[Hongseok]

29
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:37,950
[Park Seonghyeon]

30
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:42,850
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

31
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:53,450
[Play Me]

32
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:00,190
It's pouring outside.

33
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,750
Why are you here at this hour?

34
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:25,470
I should be asking you that.

35
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:27,260
What are you doing here?

36
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:29,430
Didn't your manager tell you?

37
00:02:29,430 --> 00:02:31,470
I'm sleeping here tonight.

38
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,480
Well, that's how it is.

39
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:44,110
It's pouring outside.

40
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:47,400
Are you going home by car later?

41
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,070
I can't.

42
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,540
Oh, that's right.

43
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,040
You'll call your manager, right?

44
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,870
I can't contact him.

45
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:04,210
Why? What happened?

46
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:15,470
So you're saying your car keys and phone
fell into the sewer,

47
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:17,730
and you had nowhere to go but here?

48
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:20,480
Is Seho not picking up?

49
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,310
No, he's probably asleep.

50
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:23,980
Then at least call a taxi for me.

51
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:25,900
Well, I tried,

52
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:28,570
but I couldn't get one.

53
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:30,990
Maybe because of the heavy rain.

54
00:03:30,990 --> 00:03:33,570
Then I'll wait until the rain stops.

55
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:45,210
When did you write this?

56
00:03:47,090 --> 00:03:47,750
A while ago.

57
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:55,510
Do you remember that I said I don't like
the ending of "The Little Mermaid"?

58
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:59,110
A tragic ending where you save
your loved one but die yourself...

59
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:01,390
is way too unfair.

60
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:04,980
I want to see a different ending.

61
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:07,690
One where the mermaid and her lover

62
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,860
live happily ever after.

63
00:04:11,950 --> 00:04:14,810
This script is very similar
to what we talked about.

64
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,740
Maybe it's just a coincidence.

65
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:26,870
[To K, this script is written for you.]

66
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,090
Yihyun.

67
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:38,180
Is K... me?

68
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:51,440
-Is it me?
-It doesn't matter.

69
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,820
It does matter.

70
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,320
Why?

71
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,370
Because I like you.

72
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:02,500
I've liked you since I laid eyes on you.

73
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:09,250
I was afraid
we'd drift apart if I confessed,

74
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:11,630
but I can't hide my feelings anymore.

75
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:29,020
Whether it was back then...

76
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:33,240
or now, I like you.

77
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,550
Did you sleep well?

78
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:36,510
What time is it?

79
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:41,100
Well, give me a kiss and I'll tell you.

80
00:06:50,230 --> 00:06:51,270
Sexy time.

81
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:07,410
Hey,

82
00:07:07,830 --> 00:07:10,290
why are you in the same clothes
as yesterday?

83
00:07:11,210 --> 00:07:13,710
Uh, w-well...

84
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:17,300
You worked overtime all night, didn't you?

85
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:20,380
Didn't I tell you to
take it easy with work?

86
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:22,010
Got it.

87
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:23,850
Take it easy.

88
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,930
Director Jung.

89
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,150
Director Jung?

90
00:07:32,150 --> 00:07:33,150
Yes.

91
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:37,650
If you worked overtime,
you two must've met.

92
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:39,650
Didn't Jae-on sleep here?

93
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:41,409
No!

94
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:45,159
I didn't see him at all.

95
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:47,750
Maybe because I went to bed early.

96
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:50,409
Jae-on.

97
00:07:50,409 --> 00:07:54,250
Didn't you call me in the wee hours?

98
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:57,250
D-Did... Did I?

99
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:01,380
Maybe I p-pocket-dialed you in my sleep.

100
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:04,970
Kang Jae-on!

101
00:08:04,970 --> 00:08:06,970
Do you think the theater's a hotel?

102
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,770
Hey,

103
00:08:08,770 --> 00:08:10,600
I let him sleep here.

104
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,810
He had nowhere to stay yesterday.

105
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:13,410
Everyone, focus on the play.

106
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:16,440
Stop chit-chatting about nonsense.

107
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:18,650
Don't just sleep anywhere
because you have nowhere to stay.

108
00:08:18,650 --> 00:08:20,610
Focus on your own work.

109
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,200
Got it?

110
00:08:22,530 --> 00:08:23,660
Yes.

111
00:08:34,169 --> 00:08:35,289
Are you mad at me?

112
00:08:40,669 --> 00:08:42,760
You know I didn't mean it that way.

113
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:46,050
I know. I understand, but...

114
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:50,110
How long do we have to pretend
to be on bad terms?

115
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:53,060
As long...

116
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:55,310
as possible?

117
00:08:57,860 --> 00:08:59,230
Kang Jae-on!

118
00:09:01,150 --> 00:09:02,190
Wanna have...

119
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:06,280
instant noodles before you go?

120
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,830
Will you add an egg for me?

121
00:09:18,290 --> 00:09:20,000
Ta-da.

122
00:09:23,970 --> 00:09:26,100
Woah... it looks delicious!

123
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:29,350
You even added an egg.

124
00:09:30,470 --> 00:09:32,600
I'll cook it again.

125
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:35,900
No, no!

126
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,810
I'll eat it. It looks good.

127
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,100
Give it to me.

128
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,370
Kimchi, hand.

129
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:54,120
Wow, well done.

130
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,080
Me or Kimchi?

131
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,870
Kimchi, of course.

132
00:09:56,870 --> 00:09:58,880
Kimchi only has eyes for me.

133
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:01,460
Kimchi?

134
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:02,380
Are you serious?

135
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:04,090
How could you do this to me?

136
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:05,930
Wait. Wait.

137
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:09,640
Hello?

138
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,470
I'm planning to go to your place now.

139
00:10:11,470 --> 00:10:13,100
Is there anything you want to eat?

140
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,980
Oh, now?

141
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,770
I have a guest at home.

142
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:18,900
-A guest?
-Who's it?

143
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:20,520
Who?

144
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,150
Sorry, next time then.

145
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:23,900
I'll call you back.

146
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:27,240
Hey, seriously.

147
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,330
I'm so jealous right now.

148
00:10:41,290 --> 00:10:42,460
What?

149
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:47,880
What are you doing? It tickles! Stop!

150
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:51,680
Role reversal!

151
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:54,430
It's my turn.

152
00:10:56,020 --> 00:10:57,230
How is it?

153
00:10:57,230 --> 00:10:58,230
Wait!

154
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:10,160
If only Yihyun was in the picture too.

155
00:11:19,870 --> 00:11:22,130
If you have something to say, just say it.

156
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,600
What's going on between you two?

157
00:11:34,810 --> 00:11:36,770
If this is posted online,

158
00:11:37,270 --> 00:11:38,770
what do you think

159
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,440
would happen to Jung Yihyun?

160
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:49,030
[Epilogue: Five Years Ago]

161
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:48,030
I'm on my way to your place right now.

162
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:49,860
I have something to say to you.

163
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:53,070
Can we meet up?

164
00:11:53,070 --> 00:11:56,790
Don't contact me anymore.

165
00:11:57,030 --> 00:11:58,780
[Yihyun]

166
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,100
The number you dialed cannot be reached.

167
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:05,900
Please leave a message...
